==English==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|enm|en}} {{term|silken|lang=enm}}, from {{etyl|ang|en}} {{term|seolcen||made of silk, silken|lang=ang}}, equivalent to {{suffix|silk|en|lang=en}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|en-us-silken.ogg|Audio (US)|lang=en}}

===Adjective===
{{en-adj|-}}

# Made of [[silk]].
#: ''a '''silken''' veil''
# Having a [[smooth]], [[soft]], or [[light]] [[texture]], like that of silk; [[suggestive]] of silk.
#* '''1994''', {{w|Stephen Fry}}, ''{{w|The Hippopotamus}}'', ch. 2:
#*: He heard the '''silken''' rustle of a dressing-gown being drawn on.
# {{context|figuratively|of speech, singing, [[oratory]], etc.|lang=en}} [[smooth|Smooth]]ly [[utter]]ed; [[flowing]], [[subtle]], or [[convincing]] in presentation.
#* Shakespeare
#*: '''Silken''' terms precise.
# {{context|obsolete|lang=en}} Dressed in silk.
#* Shakespeare
#*: A {{...}} '''silken''' wanton.

